>
> I have four time series with the following structure:
>
> WEEK a date variable indicating the last day of a week (on the x-axis),
>
> OUTCOME a numeric outcome variable (on the y-axis), and
>
> CAT a factor variable that differentiates the 4 variable series.
>
>
>
> I want to produce a plot with a smoothed lowess line for each level of CAT.  I can produce the line plot with LINETYPE differentiated by CAT, but I don’t see how to fit the smoothed line.
>
> I’d appreciate any suggestions how to do this.
>
>
>
> Thanks in advance
>
> AB
>
>
>
> Sample code producing the line graph below:
>
> x1<- ggplot(df, aes(x=WEEJ, y=OUTCOME, linetype=CAT)) +

You should add group=CAT to your aesthetic and maybe colour=CAT, too, so that you can distinguish them nicely.
>
>   geom_line() +
You possibly want to remove the call to geom_line() since you have data points that you want to fit. I'd use:
    geom_point() +
    geom_smooth(method="loess") +

>   scale_y_continuous("Outcome") +
>
>   scale_x_date("Week ending", breaks = date_breaks("1 week"), labels= date_format(format = "%m/%d")) +
>
>   scale_linetype_manual(name= "Category", breaks=c("LE 13","14 to 20","21 to 26", "GT 26"), values = c(10,8,5,1)) +
>
>   theme(legend.position="bottom",axis.text.x=element_text(angle=-70, hjust=0)) +
>
>   ggtitle ("Outcome by Category")

I Hope that's gives you what you wanted. You should also browse the excellent docs at http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/ for more inspiration.

Best,
Moritz

