Neither of these questions is really answerable by anyone except you--that is, we don't know what your purpose is here. Can you make *a* figure from this table? Sure. As before, start with a data frame:

d <-data.frame(community=c("Com1","Com1","Com2","Com2"), village=c("Vil1","Vil2"), gmean=c(290.05,322.54,13.67,38.14), gmedian=c(186,229,11,22))

d_melt <- melt(d,id.vars=c(1,2))

ggplot(d_melt,aes(village,value,fill=variable))+geom_bar(position="dodge",stat="identity")+facet_grid(community~.)

...but how you plot it depends on what you want to show/emphasize of course.

Ben

